course: dictionary
lesson: 2126
title: Convince: making someone believe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To convince someone is to make them believe that something is true. «No argument has convinced everyone.» Here it means that the arguments did not make every person believe the same thing.
explain: You can also convince someone to do something, which means to persuade them to do it. If you are convinced, you are completely sure. «I'm convinced that the answer is seven.»
explain: Be careful with strangers. Someone online may try to convince you to share your password or to go somewhere alone. Even if they try very hard, stop and tell an adult.
fact: Convince means to make someone believe that something is true.
fact: «Convince someone to do» something means to persuade them to do it.
fact: Convinced, as an adjective, means completely sure, as in «I'm convinced that...».
fact: «Not convinced» means you still have doubts about something.
fact: The forms are convince, convinces, convinced and convincing.
exercise: In «No argument has convinced everyone», what does convinced mean? | Made people hungry | *Made people believe something is true | Made people laugh | Made people stop talking
exercise: Tom says, «I'm convinced that the answer is seven.» What does convinced mean? | Lost | Very cold | Sleepy | *Completely sure
exercise: A stranger online tries to convince you to share your password. What should you do? | Send them your address too | Share it, because they seem nice | Tell them a joke | *Stop and tell an adult
test: Which is the best meaning of «convince someone to do something»? | To make them sad | To forget what they did | To watch them do it | *To persuade them to do it
test: Maya says, «I'm not convinced.» What does she mean? | *She still has doubts | She has already left | She is hungry | She is completely sure
exam: In «He tried to convince the judge of his innocence», what does convince mean? | Make the judge leave the court | Make the judge hungry | *Make the judge believe it is true | Make the judge laugh
